MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 68b17a837ee29b942a5a85513233c468, type: 3}
  m_Name: Intro
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  actors: 
  Dialogue:
  - '???: Wait, don''t go!'
  - 'Rat: Woah, what the- Who are ya? What are ya?'
  - As the strange being approaches your eyes focus on what appears to be a... fairy?
  - '???: I''m not a fairy! I''m far more powerful than Tooth or Bel - I''ll have
    you know. '
  - "Rat: Ya didn't answer my question, Not-Fairy.\t"
  - 'Not-Fairy: Just call me Yota for now and Yota needs you to get up... like right
    now.'
  - 'You: It''s a Saturday. I was about to take a nap- y''know?'
  - 'Yota [Not-Fairy]: You''re a rat, for Toys'' sake! You have no concept of a weekend.'
  - 'Rat: Fair point. What d''ya want, o powerful Not-Fairy?'
  - 'Yota [Not-Fairy]: You know who''s ceiling you''re living in - don''t you? I
    know rats aren''t the brightest... or the cleanest or the nicest or the - '
  - 'Rat: What''s your point?'
  - 'Yota [Not-Fairy]: Right, sorry. Stupid mouth, stupid mouth.'
  - 'Rat: Thought I was the one who ain''t "the brightest".'
  - 'Yota [Not-Fairy]: I never said I was either but that''s beside''s the point!
    Stop distracting me! I need your help with fixing something.'
  - 'Rat: Don''t know if you remember but I ain''t the brightest and I ain''t exactly
    a wiz with ma hands either, bed bug.'
  - 'Yota [Bed Bug]: That''s why I''m here! The little girl who''s room you''re living
    in - remember her? Well her toy world is disappearing. That poor girl must be
    going through something that''s destroying her imagination.'
  - 'Rat: Toy world? Uh-huh.'
  - 'Yota [Bed Bug]: Don''t you sneak in here and look at her stuff? How do you live
    in her room and not know what toys are?'
  - 'Rat: I ain''t-'
  - 'Yota [Bed Bug]: Right, right, " the brightest". You won''t let that one go -
    huh? Never mind. Point is - you have to help me - only you can. '
  - 'Rat: Oh yeah? And why''s it have to be me?'
  - 'Yota [Bed Bug]: Because! When the toy world disappears it fractures and leaks
    into the real world until nothing is left. Parts of the toy world here has already
    leaked into the real world. The other toys are from the toy world - they can''t
    touch anything in this world and well, I''m not exactly dextrous either, so enter
    Rat...'
  - 'Rat: Hmm. I get it. So, I''m the chosen hero that the whole of the toy world
    depends on, ain'' that right, fruit fly?'
  - 'Yota [Fruit Fly]: Yes! Exactly! Well, not exactly - just this little girl''s
    toy world, not the whole of the toy world. They have me for that, hehe.'
  - 'Rat: Well, that''s fine and dandy ''cept I ain''t no hero, dust mite. What''s
    in it for me?'
  - 'Yota [Dust Mite]: I''ll pretend I didn''t hear the "dust mite." '
  - 'Rat: Called ya a bed bug and a fruit fly but dust mite is crossin'' the line?'
  - 'Not-Dust-Mite-Just-Yota: You''ve never wanted to go out there? Look at this
    place - it''s nothing short of a void - I mean I can barely see you! You don''t
    have any friends or family and I can bet a wing and ring that you''re afraid
    of that little girl. When was the last you looked at anything else other than
    these four corners and a block of cheese?'
  - 'Rat: Gonna pretend I didn''t hear the "cheese'' stereotype. That''s for mice
    - by the way.'
  - 'Yota: Deflection, deflection - that''s all I hear.'
  - 'Rat: All right. All right. Might not be so bright, Yota but you''ve got keen
    observation skills. I''ll help ya.'
  - 'Yota: Yes! Thank you! If you weren''t a disease infested rodent and I wasn''t
    a holy celestial being I''d kiss you!'
  - 'Rat: Sure, thanks. Let''s just go before I change my mind.'
  - 'Yota: Right, we have no time for a break. '
  - 'Yota: Here''s what you have to do. Her toy Jenni figurine: her toy spirit  has
    already fractured into 5 pieces and leaked into the real world. You have to find
    all of her and bring her back to where her toy spirit was born before she disappears
    altogether'
  - 'Rat: Where her toy spirirt was born?'
  - 'Yota: I don''t know what it''s called in the real world but it''s where she
    stopped being just a toy and became part of a child''s imagination. Without that
    imagination there would be no toy world. Think of it as the place where Jenni
    first came out of so that our little girl and play with her for the first time.'
  - 'Yota: Once you''ve done that you need to help the mechanic. He''s fractured
    too but luckily he''s still in the toy world. Once you fix him you won''t be
    able to talk to him in this form. I''ll use my powers to help you imbue Jenni
    so you can talk to him - which is another reason why we have to get to her first.'
  - 'Rat: So, what you''re gonna use your Not-Fairy magic and turn me into a doll?'
  - "Yota: You're sarcastic but you're not far off- \n"
  - 'Rat: Ya gotta be kiddin'' me-'
  - 'Yota: Also, Jenni is a figurine, not a doll - two completely different things'
  - 'Yota: So once you return Jenni''s spirit to her place of birth you''ll be able
    to imbue her there. Your true form will remain untouched. You''ll likely want
    to go back to your true form when you need to make contact with anything in the
    real world. Just go back to the birth place when you need to change.'
  - 'Rat: How do I know what''s part of the toy world and what''s real?'
  - 'Yota: I''ve set up a barrier over the toy world to protect what''s left of it.
    As Jenni you  won''t be able to venture out of that barrier. Whatever is outside
    that barrier is the real world.'
  - 'Rat: Jeez, all right. Think I got it.'
  - 'Yota: Are you sure? Remember take Jenni''s form when you need to interact with
    other toys and go back to your true form when you need to interact with the real
    world.'
  - 'Rat: Yeah, yeah, I got it. I got it.'
